    <!-- How to play -->
    <string name="howto_title">How to play</string>
    <string name="howto_controls_title">Controls</string>
    <string name="howto_controls_body">The bowler runs in and the ball travels down the pitch. A yellow ring closes on the hitting zone in front of the batter. Tap or swipe at the moment the ring reaches the inner circle, when it flashes green.</string>
    <string name="howto_direction_title">Shot direction</string>
    <string name="howto_direction_body">Tap the left third of the pitch or swipe left to play to the leg side. Tap the middle or swipe up to hit straight. Tap the right third or swipe right for the off side. Hitting with the line (straight balls straight, outside off to the off side, balls on the pads to leg) gives you more power. Short balls can always be pulled to leg.</string>
    <string name="howto_timing_title">Timing</string>
    <string name="howto_timing_body">Perfect timing gives you full power: sixes and fours. Early or late contact still scores, mostly ones and twos. Swing outside the window and you miss. Straight balls you miss or leave will often hit the stumps. Yorkers are hard to get under, so they cost one level of power.</string>
    <string name="howto_timing_windows">Timing windows for medium pace (perfect / playable, ± milliseconds):\n%1$s\n%2$s\n%3$s\nSpinners give you about 15%% more time, fast bowlers about 10%% less.</string>
    <string name="howto_window_value">• %1$s: ±%2$d ms / ±%3$d ms</string>
    <string name="howto_field_title">Reading the field</string>
    <string name="howto_field_body">Fielders are the dots around the ground. Each over the captain picks a field. Attacking fields leave the boundary open but crowd the inner ring, so they take more catches. Boundary riders turn fours into twos and can catch big hits in the deep. Look at the gaps before the ball is bowled.</string>
    <string name="howto_scoring_title">Scoring</string>
    <string name="howto_scoring_body">Shots can score a dot, 1, 2, 3, 4 or 6. You can be out caught, bowled or run out. On a run-out you are credited the single you completed. A wide adds one run and has to be bowled again, so only six legal balls make an over.</string>
    <string name="howto_wickets_title">Wickets in short chases</string>
    <string name="howto_wickets_rule">Ten wickets would make tiny chases too easy, so the number of wickets you have depends on the overs:\n• 1 over: %1$d wickets\n• 2 overs: %2$d wickets\n• 5 overs: %3$d wickets\nYour innings ends when you reach the target, lose all your wickets or run out of balls. Finishing one run short is a tie.</string>
    <string name="howto_bowlers_title">Bowlers</string>
    <string name="howto_bowlers">• Pace: %1$d to %2$d km/h. Fast, with a little seam movement.\n• Medium: %3$d to %4$d km/h. Accurate, with some swing.\n• Spin: %5$d to %6$d km/h. Slow through the air with big turn off the pitch.\nThe game shows the bowler\'s name, type and speed before every ball.</string>
    <string name="howto_modes_title">Modes</string>
    <string name="howto_modes_body">Quick Chase gives you a random target for your overs and difficulty. Daily Challenge comes from the tournament feed: a fixed opponent, target and bowling plan that changes each day. Win it to mark it completed.</string>

